<description>&lt;p&gt;The junta is seeking US investment in rare-earth mining while China continues to rely on Myanmar’s rare-earths for its supply chains, and ASEAN pressure on the junta is increasing. The military has tightened rice shipment controls along the Taungoo-Leiktho route and the Chamber of Mines has pledged US$400,000 for Burma Camp redevelopment. Myanmar summoned the German envoy after a controversial video, and the Thai foreign minister arrived for talks with Min Aung Hlaing on border security. The army seized a key resistance headquarters and ten opposition bases, and 2,332 battle-related deaths occurred in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Business &amp;amp; Financial Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi--?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Hindu&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiuAFBVV95cUxOeGRlYnlQbHM3T3hGeWNXdHpuWWNnejNxWmVnbE1UTE1QLXFTa1BKRW9UUTdZTTJiQkxPVXR4cldabHRzdW9GUl9MbjF3YmR6czB4MUhiVWd0WFJyNXBXdVZ5U2lJdkJVOHZTMWVBY3oxbUtId1UxdENLNUVPYW1iUE5ROEpITjN1SmEzcUhuQjNBbXNiRzFYc3AwMkVRRUNnVVRxSTNOOVVVUHl0V3pGNmFLYXIwOUZY?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxNQ2pLc3RLUEFWYnlabmprNHBlQ2pkeW9Ya0hHSk54bVlXMzFDRXdSX0VUVVBIdk8wWm0xUm91ZzV5cDlSQXBRZ2RlcXBPVmRRci1ibjR5MU5Kc0ZrZ3Jtcm51S2Z4MVJMZW9ucnM3VktadElJdnRoWGhlaVpycUtpQ2RndWU2UVR3Z3pzZHpvXzBLbHpTTklwWEhhSWtTVGZ1ZXl1OHpza01GYUE?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Irrawaddy&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilgFBVV95cUxONjhhaWVjbDRjZ0NRdFVoemYxTlB4OUE2RmdQdXdIMURoZll5NEVmSnE0aXc0VUhNNzhteHRyQ1dSWkVpTE1VdGN5aXJFZWRPVGFmZGNhWHZjY1ZUeV9HY3VaVEdxc0JUME92UU4xSUk3NDMwSElTTXlCa0YxeC1CcFVGZWNEVDhkU2NheVJsS0FJMGRNdUE?oc=5